<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franz Joseph II, Prince of Liechtenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1906">1906</a>–<a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph</a> II was Prince of Liechtenstein from 1938 until his death, the first reigning prince to live permanently in the country, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaduz-castle">Vaduz Castle</a>. He kept Liechtenstein neutral in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, and during his long reign it grew from a poor farming state into a prosperous financial and industrial centre. In 1984 he handed day-to-day rule to his son Hans-Adam II.</p></div>
